{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Shimon and Levi are brothers.</b> The two of them are as one brother born for trouble. He began with their praise, in the manner of what is said (Genesis 34:25) 'And Shimon and Levi, brothers of Dinah, took' — Rashi explained that because they risked themselves for her they were called 'brothers of Dinah,' and this is indeed praise for them, that they entered the thick of the beam for the sake of their sister; but they did not act well in that they plundered the entire city, for this is instruments of violence, and vengeance does not depend on this. And because they kept a secret counsel together and assembled against the entire city, he said, 'Into their council let not my soul come; with their assembly let not my glory be joined' (Genesis 49:6) — for 'in their anger they slew a man' (Genesis 49:6). This is the reason why he began with praise: to say that they donned zealotry for the sake of their sister and killed all of them as one man. 'And in their will they uprooted a wall' (Genesis 49:6) — that is, the city wall, as the Targum renders it. And this is the reason why he concludes with condemnation, saying 'their weapons are instruments of violence' (Genesis 49:5), for this matter does not depend on anger and vengeance, but rather of their own free will they uprooted the wall to tear down the entire city and to plunder all that was theirs."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:21.238889765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}